### A1 (FATAL). Proposition 3.3 false under (P); the "global sign convention E <-> -F" patch is mathematically void, and the scratch "verification" contradicts the document

Proposition 3.3 is the single place in the paper where the cross product (SK)
is applied to a non-grouplike pair - it is the entire content of "quantum
double" for this problem. Its conclusion is
`E_iF_l - F_lE_i = delta_il (K_i - K_i''^-1)/(q-q''^-1)`. This is **inconsistent**
with the very pairing (P) the paper sets out to use.

Direct check (the same channels the paper lists, now evaluated honestly).
With theta = (q''^-1 - q)''^-1, Delta''^2(F) = (F,1,1)+(K''^-1,F,1)+(K''^-1,K''^-1,F) and
Delta''^2(E) = (EK,K,K)+(1,E,K)+(1,1,E), the double sum for cross(F,E) has
degree-1 support only at:
- (c,a): coefficient <F, EK> = theta q''^2 (Lemma 1.1(c)), leftover K;
- (b,c): coefficient -<K''^-1 F, E> * (grouplike channel = 1) = -theta,
  leftover K''^-1.
Everything else dies by Lemma 1.1(e). Hence, abstractly under the axioms (P),
   (SK)   F E - E F = theta q''^2 K - theta K''^-1 .
Now use q''^2 theta = -theta (since theta(q - q''^-1) = -1 exactly):
   (SK)   F E - E F = -theta K - theta K''^-1,
   i.e.   [E,F] = theta(K + K''^-1) .                              (SK-sign)

But (H1) of the paper says K E K''^-1 = q''^2 E, so the specialization
K''^-1 |-> q''^2 K must be an algebra map of the presented double D. Applied to
the SK result it gives -theta K - theta(q''^2 K) = -theta(1+q''^2)K, nonzero;
applied to (H2) it gives theta(1 - q''^2)K = K. The two presentations define
**different algebras**. Claiming (H2) as the cross relation while keeping (P)
as the pairing is a contradiction; one of them must change.

The paper'"'s patch - the sentence \"... which is (H2) **up to the global sign
convention E <-> -F**\" - is void: under E |-> -E, F |-> -F the commutator
[E,F] |-> [E,F] is fixed (two sign flips), so no \"sign convention\" can turn
theta(K + K"'^-1) into theta(K - K''^-1). This is confidence language
substituting for proof (AC-3 negative test; plan.md: "never present
conjecture as fact ... an invented theorem or concealed gap").

